From d7f4ef1071fe74705b168f72ced4c00ca7d8bd3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Frdlik <michaelf.ms@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 10:54:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] Thylacine Warp V-3b-3c-2b re-audit (F4/F5/F6/F7):
 placed-map + errno discrimination

The dirty-close re-audit (holotype Fable 5, I-45 client, on the 2c742991 fix
state) returned 0 P0 / 1 P1 / 2 P2 / 1 P3. All fixed; the E2E re-witnessed GREEN
on real V3D (thyla-pi/KVM, Venus V3D 4.2.14): device-memory sentinel OK ->
THYLACINE-VENUS-PROVE PASS, with the logical device created against the now
de-advertised placed-map extension.

- F4 [P1]: VK_EXT_map_memory_placed was advertised (memoryMapPlaced=true)
  unconditionally, but thylacine_bo_map discarded pPlacedAddress (weft picks the
  VA) -> a placed map would silently succeed at the WRONG address (app
  corruption). Fix: a new vn_renderer_info.cannot_map_placed bit (Thylacine sets
  it) suppresses the extension + feature in vn_physical_device; plus a defensive
  refuse in thylacine_bo_map (a caller that sets the PLACED bit without the
  feature gets a clean VK_ERROR_MEMORY_MAP_FAILED, never the wrong VA).

- F5 [P2] + F6 [P2] invariant-break: warp_mem_new's rc=1 ("free the handle") was
  "the write failed", not "the server refused". Two ways that frees a handle
  whose server slot IS installed -> a re-handed handle collides -> the instance-
  wide vkAllocateMemory wedge F2 was meant to close: (F5) an -EINTR after the
  Twrite committed (LATENT until native readers become caught-interruptible, the
  planned 11c); (F6) a concurrent-alloc race loser's duplicate -EINVAL. Fix:
  warp_mem_new inspects the real errno (dev9p propagates the Rlerror ecode) and
  frees ONLY on provably-not-installed -- an open failure or the routine -ENOMEM
  holistic-cap refusal; every other failure (-EINVAL/-EINTR/short/unknown) keeps
  the handle marked. This closes F5 and F6's invariant-break; F6's residual
  torn-RMW on the bitmap is the owed per-renderer mutex (comment re-scoped: the
  trigger is ANY concurrent vkAllocateMemory, not multi-queue).

  NOTE the divergence from the round-2 remedy: the prosecutor's suggested F5 fix
  put -EINVAL in the free set. That reproduces F6 (a duplicate -EINVAL means the
  slot IS installed, so freeing frees the winner's slot). The reconciled
  predicate frees ONLY on provably-not-installed (open-fail / -ENOMEM) and keeps
  on everything else -- the conservative direction that closes both F5 and F6's
  invariant-break. The prosecutor is authoritative about the smell, not the
  remedy.

- F7 [P3]: the bo-create comment misdocumented the binding as
  VkImportMemoryResourceInfoMESA (unreachable here); reworded to the real
  mechanism (host resolves blob_id=mem_id; wait_alloc's WaitRingSeqno orders it).

Re-witnessed: build rc=0 on thyla-keep, prove md5 c0ccddda -> e386bc27, ramfs
sha verified on the pi, THYLACINE-VENUS-PROVE PASS. The fix PROOFS (F4 placed-
refusal, F5 EINTR-keep, F6 concurrent-alloc, F5 ENOMEM-still-frees) need error-
path witnesses owed at the GPU-submit chunk; this E2E confirms the happy path +
device creation with the de-advertised extension.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
